{
    "background_story": "Bentley, a language enthusiast, had always been fascinated by the rich cultural heritage of India. During his travels, he stumbled upon the Kannada language, spoken by millions in the southern state of Karnataka. Entranced by its melodic sound and complex script, Bentley devoted himself to mastering Kannada. He spent years studying the language, pouring over texts and practicing with native speakers. As he delved deeper, he discovered the works of renowned Kannada poets and writers, whose words resonated deeply with him. Bentley's love for Kannada eventually led him to become a translator, helping to introduce the language's literary treasures to a global audience. His dedication earned him the respect and admiration of the Kannada community, who welcomed him as one of their own.",
